# Batch request error handling

## Problem

The backend `batch_requests` API runs sub-requests in series in one atomic transaction. If one sub-request fails, the backend returns a 4xx/5xx status for the full batch. The response body is `{ results: [{ reference_id, status_code, data }] }` — each sub-result keeps its own `status_code`, and failed sub-results carry their error body in `data`.

The global error handler (`handleHttpError`) does not know this shape. On a batch failure it falls into `handleStructuredErrors`, iterates the `results` array, finds no known error fields on successful entries, and toasts "something went wrong" for every entry — including the successful ones.

## Approach

Update `useBatchRequest` (`src/Utils/request/batch.ts`) in place. No call-site changes needed for the 4 existing consumers.

Wrap the existing `mutate(...)` call in the `mutationFn` with a try/catch:

1. Catch only `HTTPError` whose `cause` is a batch response (`results` is an array of objects with `reference_id` and `status_code`). Re-throw anything else untouched.
2. For each failed sub-result (`status_code > 299`), build a synthetic `HTTPError` with `status = sub status_code` and `cause = sub data`, and pass it to the global `handleHttpError`. Sub-errors thus get full existing treatment: pydantic errors, structured errors, 404 detail, session expiry, etc. Successful sub-results produce no toast.
3. Mark the original error `silent = true` and re-throw it. The global mutation cache `onError` skips silent errors, but the mutation still enters error state and consumer `onError`/`onSettled` callbacks still fire with the original error (batch results accessible via `error.cause.results`).

Also support an optional `silent` flag on `useBatchRequest` options: when set, skip step 2 (no per-sub-error toasts) for consumers that fully handle errors themselves.

### Sketch

```ts
function isBatchResponse(cause): cause is BatchRequestResponse {
  return Array.isArray(cause?.results) && cause.results.every(
    (r) => typeof r === "object" && "reference_id" in r && "status_code" in r);
}

mutationFn: async (requests) => {
  try {
    return await mutate(batchRoute)({ requests: ... });
  } catch (error) {
    if (!(error instanceof HTTPError) || !isBatchResponse(error.cause)) throw error;
    if (!silent) {
      for (const r of error.cause.results.filter((r) => r.status_code > 299)) {
        handleHttpError(new HTTPError({
          message: "Request Failed",
          status: r.status_code,
          silent: false,
          cause: r.data as Record<string, unknown>,
        }));
      }
    }
    error.silent = true;
    throw error;
  }
}
```

No change to `errorHandler.ts` or `queryClient.ts`.

## Files

- `src/Utils/request/batch.ts` — add try/catch, `isBatchResponse` guard, per-sub-error dispatch, `silent` option. JSDoc in ASD-STE100 simplified technical English.
- `src/Utils/request/README.md` — add a `useBatchRequest` section (usage + error behavior). Do not touch existing content. ASD-STE100 simplified technical English.

## Todos

1. Update `useBatchRequest` in `src/Utils/request/batch.ts` with per-sub-response error handling.
2. Add `useBatchRequest` documentation to `src/Utils/request/README.md`.
3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` and lint on changed files.

## Notes

- `HTTPError.silent` is mutable; `handleHttpError` checks `"silent" in error && error.silent`, so marking the original error silent before re-throwing suppresses the global fallback toast while consumer callbacks still run.
- Consumers with custom `onError` (e.g. `DispensedMedicationList`) keep working; they can pass `silent: true` if they do not want the per-sub-error toasts.
- The 500 (`UnHandledError`) case is covered too: the failed sub-result has no `data`, so the synthetic error falls back to the generic toast; earlier successful sub-results are skipped.

